window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst used the following model in analyzing product features from the viewpoint of the customer. What technique did the business analysis use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kano Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Kano Analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>MoSCoW Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. MoSCoW Analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feature Model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Feature Model\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Purpose Alignment Model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Purpose Alignment Model\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Kano model is an approach to prioritizing product functionalities based on their implementation cost versus their potential to satisfy customers (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 79, 80).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Kano model is an approach to prioritizing product functionalities based on their implementation cost versus their potential to satisfy customers (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 79, 80).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"mock-1\",\"title\":\"Full Mock Exam 1\",\"kind\":\"Full Mock Exam\",\"count\":150,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In an interior design project for a library, the client asks the team to increase the number of bookshelves beyond what was agreed on. Since the project is on schedule and adding additional shelves will make no difference, the project manager consents to the client’s request. This is an example of:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In an interior design project for a library, the client asks the team to increase the number of bookshelves beyond what was agreed on. Since the project is on schedule and adding additional shelves will make no difference, the project manager consents to the client’s request. This is an example of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gold Plating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Gold Plating\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Customer Obsession<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Customer Obsession\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope Creep<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scope Creep\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Successful Project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Successful Project\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Scope creep (also known as “feature creep” or “requirement creep”) refers to the uncontrolled expansion of the project’s scope (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The tackled situation is not considered gold plating since the client is the one who brought up the change request; it was neither the project manager nor team members who added changes without the client’s approval, as gold plating implies.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Customer obsession consists of an excessive focus on providing a better customer experience by meeting and even exceeding your client’s needs. However, customer obsession shouldn’t mean delivering beyond scope since the latter can increase the project schedule and cost, thus decreasing the success rate of the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Scope creep (also known as “feature creep” or “requirement creep”) refers to the uncontrolled expansion of the project’s scope (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249). Option A: The tackled situation is not considered gold plating since the client is the one who brought up the change request; it was neither the project manager nor team members who added changes without the client’s approval, as gold plating implies. Option B: Customer obsession consists of an excessive focus on providing a better customer experience by meeting and even exceeding your client’s needs. However, customer obsession shouldn’t mean delivering beyond scope since the latter can increase the project schedule and cost, thus decreasing the success rate of the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which tool ensures that each solution requirement is linked to the business needs, goals, and objectives, as well as stakeholder expectations?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool ensures that each solution requirement is linked to the business needs, goals, and objectives, as well as stakeholder expectations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements traceability matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Requirements traceability matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders engagement assessment matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholders engagement assessment matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Readiness assessment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Readiness assessment\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>MoSCoW<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. MoSCoW\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The requirements traceability matrix ensures that each solution requirement is valuable and within scope by linking it to business needs, goals, and project objectives. RTM verifies that solution requirements align with stakeholder expectations by tracing them back to stakeholder requirements. RTM is typically used in a predictive environment.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Stakeholders engagement assessment matrix is used to compare the current engagement against the desired engagement level.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A readiness assessment evaluates an organization’s preparedness to transition a solution to maintenance and operations. It involves a thorough analysis of readiness across all areas, identifying gaps that pose risks to achieving the desired outcome, and developing responses to address these risks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> MoSCoW is a prioritization technique used to categorize requirements into four groups: \\\"Must Have,\\\" \\\"Should Have,\\\" \\\"Could Have,\\\" and \\\"Won't Have.\\\" This method helps business analysts prioritize features and functions, ensuring that resources are allocated to the most valuable aspects of a project. MoSCoW can be applied in predictive, hybrid, and adaptive project environments.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The requirements traceability matrix ensures that each solution requirement is valuable and within scope by linking it to business needs, goals, and project objectives. RTM verifies that solution requirements align with stakeholder expectations by tracing them back to stakeholder requirements. RTM is typically used in a predictive environment. Option B: Stakeholders engagement assessment matrix is used to compare the current engagement against the desired engagement level. Option C: A readiness assessment evaluates an organization’s preparedness to transition a solution to maintenance and operations. It involves a thorough analysis of readiness across all areas, identifying gaps that pose risks to achieving the desired outcome, and developing responses to address these risks. Option D: MoSCoW is a prioritization technique used to categorize requirements into four groups: \\\"Must Have,\\\" \\\"Should Have,\\\" \\\"Could Have,\\\" and \\\"Won't Have.\\\" This method helps business analysts prioritize features and functions, ensuring that resources are allocated to the most valuable aspects of a project. MoSCoW can be applied in predictive, hybrid, and adaptive project environments.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A team, with no defined roles, uses a board and cards to categorize tasks into “To do”, “Doing”, and “Done”. Without too many restrictions, team members grab a card from the “To do” list and begin to work. What agile framework is being described?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A team, with no defined roles, uses a board and cards to categorize tasks into “To do”, “Doing”, and “Done”. Without too many restrictions, team members grab a card from the “To do” list and begin to work. What agile framework is being described?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Kanban\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lean<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Lean\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kaizen<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Kaizen\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Kanban is an agile method that employs a pull-based work system where tasks are assigned only when resources are available.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Unlike Scrum, the Kanban team has no formal roles. Additionally, Kanban practice has fewer restrictions than Scrum.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Lean is not an agile framework. In contrast, agile and kanban are subsets of lean (Agile Practice Guide, page 11)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Kaizen is a quality and resource management philosophy of applying continuous small improvements to increase productivity and reduce costs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Kanban is an agile method that employs a pull-based work system where tasks are assigned only when resources are available. Option A: Unlike Scrum, the Kanban team has no formal roles. Additionally, Kanban practice has fewer restrictions than Scrum. Option C: Lean is not an agile framework. In contrast, agile and kanban are subsets of lean (Agile Practice Guide, page 11) . Option D: Kaizen is a quality and resource management philosophy of applying continuous small improvements to increase productivity and reduce costs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sPW-0\\\">The stakeholder engagement process involves five steps. Add the following steps to the figure below: <span>Identify<\\/span>, <span>Monitor<\\/span>, <span>Engage<\\/span>, and <span>Understand &amp; analyze<\\/span>.<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\" id=\\\"page_55\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"The stakeholder engagement process involves five steps. Add the following steps to the figure below: Identify , Monitor , Engage , and Understand & analyze .\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<div class=\\\"class_s27Z-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">A. Identify B. Understand &amp; analyze C. Engage D. Monitor<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">(PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 10). Stakeholders’ engagement starts by identifying all parties directly or indirectly connected or involved in the project. Next, the identified stakeholders must be fully understood in terms of their beliefs, attitudes, expectations, etc. towards the project in order to be able to analyze each one’s level of power, interest, impact, etc., and prioritize them accordingly. After that, an engagement plan is created according to the findings of the previous steps, where a project manager should ensure clear and constant communication, the satisfaction of stakeholders’ requirements and expectations, and issue resolution when needed. Monitoring stakeholders is the final step in the process, and it entails monitoring any changes in their attitudes or power levels to adapt the engagement plan accordingly.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"A. Identify B. Understand & analyze C. Engage D. Monitor (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 10). Stakeholders’ engagement starts by identifying all parties directly or indirectly connected or involved in the project. Next, the identified stakeholders must be fully understood in terms of their beliefs, attitudes, expectations, etc. towards the project in order to be able to analyze each one’s level of power, interest, impact, etc., and prioritize them accordingly. After that, an engagement plan is created according to the findings of the previous steps, where a project manager should ensure clear and constant communication, the satisfaction of stakeholders’ requirements and expectations, and issue resolution when needed. Monitoring stakeholders is the final step in the process, and it entails monitoring any changes in their attitudes or power levels to adapt the engagement plan accordingly.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"]],\"options\":[[\"identify\",\"Identify\"],[\"monitor\",\"Monitor\"],[\"engage\",\"Engage\"],[\"understand\",\"Understand & analyze\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"identify\",\"B\":\"understand\",\"C\":\"engage\",\"D\":\"monitor\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What is the purpose of a project charter?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the purpose of a project charter?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To document the project approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To document the project approach\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To formally authorize the project and document its initial requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To formally authorize the project and document its initial requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To be used as a reference during the project kick-off meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To be used as a reference during the project kick-off meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To set up the project code of conduct<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To set up the project code of conduct\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project charter is used to formally authorize both the project manager to start the project, as well as document the project’s objectives and its high-level scope. It also defines the responsibilities and roles of all involved parties in the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A project charter is used to formally authorize both the project manager to start the project, as well as document the project’s objectives and its high-level scope. It also defines the responsibilities and roles of all involved parties in the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Before announcing the completion of the project execution, the project manager of a construction project reviews deliverables and performs a site walkthrough. What is the project manager performing in this scenario?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Before announcing the completion of the project execution, the project manager of a construction project reviews deliverables and performs a site walkthrough. What is the project manager performing in this scenario?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​An inspection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. An inspection\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​A handing over<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A handing over\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​An audit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. An audit\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A scope validation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A scope validation\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During an inspection, the project manager reviews deliverables and performs a site walkthrough if applicable.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> The project manager here is neither validating the scope with the customer nor handing over deliverables to them<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Audits are carried out to determine if project activities comply with organizational and project policies, processes, and procedures (PMI - Process groups guide, page 248). In other words, audits are performed on processes while inspections are performed on products.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A During an inspection, the project manager reviews deliverables and performs a site walkthrough if applicable. Options B & D: The project manager here is neither validating the scope with the customer nor handing over deliverables to them . Option C: Audits are carried out to determine if project activities comply with organizational and project policies, processes, and procedures (PMI - Process groups guide, page 248). In other words, audits are performed on processes while inspections are performed on products.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In a project context, guidelines and policies are classified as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a project context, guidelines and policies are classified as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Regulations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Regulations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Best practices<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Best practices\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assumptions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Assumptions\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Constraints\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">​Project constraints are restrictions that limit the project in a certain way. A cost restriction, for instance, means that the project is limited by its allocated budget or resources. Other constraints include policies, standards, guidelines, etc.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Project constraints are restrictions that limit the project in a certain way. A cost restriction, for instance, means that the project is limited by its allocated budget or resources. Other constraints include policies, standards, guidelines, etc.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">To compare the different suppliers and make the best choice, which of the following tools or techniques should the project manager use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To compare the different suppliers and make the best choice, which of the following tools or techniques should the project manager use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Procurement performance review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Procurement performance review\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Selection criteri<span><\\/span>a<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Selection criteri a\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Procurement audit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Procurement audit\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Make or buy analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Make or buy analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">It's essential for both the project manager and the project team to create selection criteria to rate and score proposals from the suppliers. In the case of a bid or quote, the price offered by the seller represents the main evaluation criterion. In other cases involving proposals, the evaluation criteria can include various aspects such as the seller’s experience, references, certifications, etc.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> In this scenario, the project manager has received proposals, so a make-or-buy analysis should have been already carried out at this point.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options C &amp; A:<\\/span> An audit or a performance review should take place at a later stage to verify that all procurement processes were respected and that the purchased items conform to requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B It's essential for both the project manager and the project team to create selection criteria to rate and score proposals from the suppliers. In the case of a bid or quote, the price offered by the seller represents the main evaluation criterion. In other cases involving proposals, the evaluation criteria can include various aspects such as the seller’s experience, references, certifications, etc. Option D: In this scenario, the project manager has received proposals, so a make-or-buy analysis should have been already carried out at this point. Options C & A: An audit or a performance review should take place at a later stage to verify that all procurement processes were respected and that the purchased items conform to requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The following are not a Business Analyst’s responsibilities, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The following are not a Business Analyst’s responsibilities, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Eliciting, analyzing, and documenting stakeholders requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Eliciting, analyzing, and documenting stakeholders requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​QA testing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. QA testing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Managing the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Managing the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Backlog prioritization<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Backlog prioritization\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Eliciting, analyzing, and documenting stakeholders' requirements is a core responsibility of a business analyst. They work to gather detailed requirements from stakeholders, analyze these requirements to understand their implications, and document them to ensure clarity and alignment.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> QA Testing may be the responsibility of the project team in identifying defects in the product and ensuring it meets quality standards.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Managing the project is the project manager’s primary responsibility.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Backlog prioritization is the product owner’s responsibility.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Eliciting, analyzing, and documenting stakeholders' requirements is a core responsibility of a business analyst. They work to gather detailed requirements from stakeholders, analyze these requirements to understand their implications, and document them to ensure clarity and alignment. Option B: QA Testing may be the responsibility of the project team in identifying defects in the product and ensuring it meets quality standards. Option C: Managing the project is the project manager’s primary responsibility. Option D: Backlog prioritization is the product owner’s responsibility.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project involves dozens of stakeholders. Most of them need high-level information and updates about the project status, while the rest need more detailed information and frequent updates. Therefore, the project manager decides to set up an action plan to respond to these different requirements. What should the project manager create?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project involves dozens of stakeholders. Most of them need high-level information and updates about the project status, while the rest need more detailed information and frequent updates. Therefore, the project manager decides to set up an action plan to respond to these different requirements. What should the project manager create?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Power/interest grid<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Power/interest grid\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder engagement plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A stakeholder engagement plan sets up strategies and actions to ensure the positive and effective involvement of all stakeholders in the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 187).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The stakeholder register lists the project stakeholders and doesn’t include any action plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> The power/interest grid and stakeholder engagement assessment matrix are tools and techniques to analyze stakeholders and assess their level of engagement. Unlike the stakeholder engagement plan, these tools do not generate or comprise practical information on how to engage and monitor stakeholders such as the frequency of official meetings, recipients of status reports, communication channels, etc<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A stakeholder engagement plan sets up strategies and actions to ensure the positive and effective involvement of all stakeholders in the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 187). Option B: The stakeholder register lists the project stakeholders and doesn’t include any action plan. Options A & D: The power/interest grid and stakeholder engagement assessment matrix are tools and techniques to analyze stakeholders and assess their level of engagement. Unlike the stakeholder engagement plan, these tools do not generate or comprise practical information on how to engage and monitor stakeholders such as the frequency of official meetings, recipients of status reports, communication channels, etc .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager has been assigned to a 300 ft farm fencing project. Having previously managed two similar projects in another region, the project manager knows that the materials for a chain-link fence cost $10 per foot, while labor costs range from $10 to $15 per linear foot, depending on the workers' experience and common rates in the region. What is the best way to estimate the labor cost per linear foot?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been assigned to a 300 ft farm fencing project. Having previously managed two similar projects in another region, the project manager knows that the materials for a chain-link fence cost $10 per foot, while labor costs range from $10 to $15 per linear foot, depending on the workers' experience and common rates in the region. What is the best way to estimate the labor cost per linear foot?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Three-point estimation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Three-point estimation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Parametric estimating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Parametric estimating\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Bottom-up estimating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Bottom-up estimating\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analogous estimating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Analogous estimating\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The three-point estimating is the triangular distribution of pessimistic, optimistic, and most likely estimates. This technique is used when there is insufﬁcient historical data or when there is only judgmental data.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Parametric estimating can be used to estimate the cost of the 300 ft fence after figuring out the labor cost per linear foot.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Bottom-up estimating can’t be used in this situation since the labor cost depends on the workers’ experience and the applied rates in the region, not on the volume and decomposition of the required work.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Since the two similar projects were performed in another region, the project manager can’t precisely define the labor cost using analogous estimating.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The three-point estimating is the triangular distribution of pessimistic, optimistic, and most likely estimates. This technique is used when there is insufﬁcient historical data or when there is only judgmental data. Option B: Parametric estimating can be used to estimate the cost of the 300 ft fence after figuring out the labor cost per linear foot. Option C: Bottom-up estimating can’t be used in this situation since the labor cost depends on the workers’ experience and the applied rates in the region, not on the volume and decomposition of the required work. Option D: Since the two similar projects were performed in another region, the project manager can’t precisely define the labor cost using analogous estimating.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A Business Analyst for a large construction project works with the project manager to define the steps to perform stakeholder analysis. Which of the following correctly defines the steps for stakeholder analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Business Analyst for a large construction project works with the project manager to define the steps to perform stakeholder analysis. Which of the following correctly defines the steps for stakeholder analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and document stakeholder information, create a communications management plan, and plan for stakeholder management.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identify and document stakeholder information, create a communications management plan, and plan for stakeholder management.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and create the communications management plan for stakeholder management.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and create the communications management plan for stakeholder management.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and plan for stakeholder management.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and plan for stakeholder management.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create a focus group for known stakeholders, identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and plan for stakeholder management<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create a focus group for known stakeholders, identify and document the stakeholder information, prioritize and classify the stakeholders, and plan for stakeholder management .\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Stakeholder analysis starts with identifying and documenting the stakeholders’ contact information, knowledge, expectations of the project, and their level of influence over project decisions. Then the business analyst works with the project manager to prioritize and classify stakeholders based on their power, influence, expectations, and concerns for the project. Finally, the business analyst should plan for managing the stakeholders based on possible negative or positive scenarios in the project that may affect the stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Stakeholder analysis starts with identifying and documenting the stakeholders’ contact information, knowledge, expectations of the project, and their level of influence over project decisions. Then the business analyst works with the project manager to prioritize and classify stakeholders based on their power, influence, expectations, and concerns for the project. Finally, the business analyst should plan for managing the stakeholders based on possible negative or positive scenarios in the project that may affect the stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was assigned to a large project that had unclear requirements and deliverables. After choosing an agile approach to deal with the situation, what should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was assigned to a large project that had unclear requirements and deliverables. After choosing an agile approach to deal with the situation, what should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acquire an agile coach to clarify the project scope.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acquire an agile coach to clarify the project scope.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitate the identification and prioritization of current work items, then ensure their execution in an iterative and incremental way.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Facilitate the identification and prioritization of current work items, then ensure their execution in an iterative and incremental way.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Set up a cross-functional team to help define all the needed iterations for completing the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Set up a cross-functional team to help define all the needed iterations for completing the project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Have a meeting with the product owner or sponsor to discuss project baselines.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Have a meeting with the product owner or sponsor to discuss project baselines.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should start by facilitating the identification and prioritization of evident requirements, hence helping with the elaboration of the product backlog. Next, and since the project is following an agile approach, the project manager should execute work iteratively and incrementally.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Since the project is large and deliverables are vague, it might not be possible to make the project scope clearer and remove ambiguity before starting implementation. In that case, the predictive approach would be more suitable than agile. Needless to say the agile coach’s role does not involve clarifying the scope of work, it rather entails helping the project team embrace an agile mindset.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Defining all of the iterations needed for completing the project refers to predictive planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Project baselines are only specified in predictive projects.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager should start by facilitating the identification and prioritization of evident requirements, hence helping with the elaboration of the product backlog. Next, and since the project is following an agile approach, the project manager should execute work iteratively and incrementally. Option A: Since the project is large and deliverables are vague, it might not be possible to make the project scope clearer and remove ambiguity before starting implementation. In that case, the predictive approach would be more suitable than agile. Needless to say the agile coach’s role does not involve clarifying the scope of work, it rather entails helping the project team embrace an agile mindset. Option C: Defining all of the iterations needed for completing the project refers to predictive planning. Option D: Project baselines are only specified in predictive projects.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager who adopts a servant leadership style is onboarding a new team member. The project manager gives the team member a copy of the project charter and commits to sending them a copy of ________________, which covers team values, ground rules, and working agreements.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager who adopts a servant leadership style is onboarding a new team member. The project manager gives the team member a copy of the project charter and commits to sending them a copy of ________________, which covers team values, ground rules, and working agreements.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The employment contract<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The employment contract\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The resource management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The resource management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The communication management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The communication management plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The team charter\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A team charter is a document that is developed in a group setting to clarify team direction while also establishing boundaries. It is created at the team’s forming phase in order to encourage <span><\\/span>understanding and buy-in. A team charter aligns the team with ground rules, team values, meeting guidelines, working agreements, as well as other group norms (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 192).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A team charter is a document that is developed in a group setting to clarify team direction while also establishing boundaries. It is created at the team’s forming phase in order to encourage understanding and buy-in. A team charter aligns the team with ground rules, team values, meeting guidelines, working agreements, as well as other group norms (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 192).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project has been hampered by many quality issues, putting the project at risk. Which meeting should the project manager conduct with the team to figure out how to avoid or deal with such problems in the future?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project has been hampered by many quality issues, putting the project at risk. Which meeting should the project manager conduct with the team to figure out how to avoid or deal with such problems in the future?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kick-off<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Kick-off\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Lessons learned\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk review\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team building<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Team building\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Lessons learned meetings are collaborative retrospective sessions for discussing, documenting, and soliciting feedback about the project's successes and missteps. These meetings are a must for the project team to learn from previous mistakes and improve future processes and projects. Lessons learned meetings should be held whenever needed, to review the way a project has been progressing, note important learnings, and set new ways for amelioration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Kick-off meetings are meant for communicating the objectives of the project and ensuring the stakeholders’ commitment to the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Risk review meetings are used to verify the status of existing risks and identify new ones (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180). However, capturing lessons learned from current or closed risks commonly happens in the lessons learned meetings.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Team building activities aim to increase collaboration among team members.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Lessons learned meetings are collaborative retrospective sessions for discussing, documenting, and soliciting feedback about the project's successes and missteps. These meetings are a must for the project team to learn from previous mistakes and improve future processes and projects. Lessons learned meetings should be held whenever needed, to review the way a project has been progressing, note important learnings, and set new ways for amelioration. Option A: Kick-off meetings are meant for communicating the objectives of the project and ensuring the stakeholders’ commitment to the project. Option C: Risk review meetings are used to verify the status of existing risks and identify new ones (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 180). However, capturing lessons learned from current or closed risks commonly happens in the lessons learned meetings. Option D: Team building activities aim to increase collaboration among team members.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the project planning phase, stakeholders insisted that their conflicting requirements should all be considered and consolidated. That made it hard for the project manager to create a plan that satisfied all stakeholders. What should the project manager do to establish a common ground?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the project planning phase, stakeholders insisted that their conflicting requirements should all be considered and consolidated. That made it hard for the project manager to create a plan that satisfied all stakeholders. What should the project manager do to establish a common ground?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Build focus groups involving concerned stakeholders to discuss and resolve conflicting interests.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Build focus groups involving concerned stakeholders to discuss and resolve conflicting interests.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create a document explaining their personal point of view and ask conflicting stakeholders to review it.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Create a document explaining their personal point of view and ask conflicting stakeholders to review it.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Give each stakeholder the opportunity to write a statement of work, and then merge all documents to create the project scope statement.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Give each stakeholder the opportunity to write a statement of work, and then merge all documents to create the project scope statement.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use their authorization and position as the project manager to decide which requirements should be prioritized.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Use their authorization and position as the project manager to decide which requirements should be prioritized.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Focus groups bring together stakeholders and subject matter experts to interactively discuss and learn about their expectations and attitudes towards a proposed service, product, or result (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 15).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Focus groups bring together stakeholders and subject matter experts to interactively discuss and learn about their expectations and attitudes towards a proposed service, product, or result (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 15).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Regardless of the type of development approach that a project manager adopts for their project, their top priority should always be:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Regardless of the type of development approach that a project manager adopts for their project, their top priority should always be:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Up-to-date documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Up-to-date documentation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Efficient collaboration and strong relationships with all project stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Efficient collaboration and strong relationships with all project stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Satisfying customers by fulfilling project requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Satisfying customers by fulfilling project requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Elaborating a robust plan and responding to change requests<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Elaborating a robust plan and responding to change requests\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In any business, customers or sponsors have to be the highest priority when delivering a product. It’s not enough to deliver a functioning product; the product must work for the customer or the sponsor’s needs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In any business, customers or sponsors have to be the highest priority when delivering a product. It’s not enough to deliver a functioning product; the product must work for the customer or the sponsor’s needs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">One year into managing a predictive project, and during the close project process, the project manager faces a key stakeholder’s refusal to sign off the deliverables due to non-compliance claims. What can the project manager do to ensure stakeholder acceptance?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"One year into managing a predictive project, and during the close project process, the project manager faces a key stakeholder’s refusal to sign off the deliverables due to non-compliance claims. What can the project manager do to ensure stakeholder acceptance?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Issue a change request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Issue a change request\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Conduct a sprint retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Conduct a sprint retrospective\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Change the SOW<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Change the SOW\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Conduct a variance analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conduct a variance analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Variance analysis is a technique used at the end of a project or phase in order to identify any deviation in deliverables or difference between actual and planned behaviors. This method is used to determine the cause and magnitude of the difference between baseline and actual performance, as well as retain control over the project (PMBOK 7th edition, page 177 &amp; PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 278)<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Variance analysis is a technique used at the end of a project or phase in order to identify any deviation in deliverables or difference between actual and planned behaviors. This method is used to determine the cause and magnitude of the difference between baseline and actual performance, as well as retain control over the project (PMBOK 7th edition, page 177 & PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 278)\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">In a projectized organization structure, after getting the client’s approval of deliverables and officially closing the project, what should be the project manager's next step? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a projectized organization structure, after getting the client’s approval of deliverables and officially closing the project, what should be the project manager's next step?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Perform a final quality inspection.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Perform a final quality inspection.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the functional manager so they can assign the team to another project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Inform the functional manager so they can assign the team to another project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check for any pending or incomplete tasks.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Check for any pending or incomplete tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Release the project team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Release the project team.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-1\\\">In projectized organizations, all activities are managed through projects. Upon completion of the project, the project manager releases the team members to move on to the next project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Quality inspections are performed before getting the client’s approval<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Unlike functional organizations, projectized organizations have no functional managers, and if they do, their role and authority are quite limited.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Checking whether all project tasks are completed should be also carried out before delivering the final product to the client since it’s part of the quality audit.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In projectized organizations, all activities are managed through projects. Upon completion of the project, the project manager releases the team members to move on to the next project. Option A: Quality inspections are performed before getting the client’s approval . Option B: Unlike functional organizations, projectized organizations have no functional managers, and if they do, their role and authority are quite limited. Option C: Checking whether all project tasks are completed should be also carried out before delivering the final product to the client since it’s part of the quality audit.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager keeps receiving negative feedback concerning one of the project suppliers. The conflicts between the project team and the supplier’s team are getting worse recently and are starting to have a negative impact on the project. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager keeps receiving negative feedback concerning one of the project suppliers. The conflicts between the project team and the supplier’s team are getting worse recently and are starting to have a negative impact on the project. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Send an email to the supplier’s team manager explaining the alarming situation.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Send an email to the supplier’s team manager explaining the alarming situation.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Meet with the supplier’s team manager to discuss the issue.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Meet with the supplier’s team manager to discuss the issue.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Call the supplier’s team manager and urge them to commit to the procurement agreement.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Call the supplier’s team manager and urge them to commit to the procurement agreement.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Proceed with Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR).\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">When you want to resolve a conflict, a face-to-face meeting is always the best first step. Hence, the project manager should meet with the manager of the supplier’s team to discuss the issue and try to find a solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Other communication methods, such as sending an email or having a phone call, are less effective than an in-person meeting.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> If direct negotiation fails, then the project manager should proceed with Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR), such as mediation or arbitration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B When you want to resolve a conflict, a face-to-face meeting is always the best first step. Hence, the project manager should meet with the manager of the supplier’s team to discuss the issue and try to find a solution. Option A: Other communication methods, such as sending an email or having a phone call, are less effective than an in-person meeting. Option D: If direct negotiation fails, then the project manager should proceed with Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR), such as mediation or arbitration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">For the next release, the product owner has selected a number of user stories totaling 110 points. Given that the team’s velocity is 20 story points, what’s the estimated duration to complete this release?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"For the next release, the product owner has selected a number of user stories totaling 110 points. Given that the team’s velocity is 20 story points, what’s the estimated duration to complete this release?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>5 sprints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 5 sprints\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>5.5 sprints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 5.5 sprints\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>6 sprints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 6 sprints\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It’s not possible to calculate the estimated number of sprints to complete a release in Agile.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It’s not possible to calculate the estimated number of sprints to complete a release in Agile.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A release of 110 story points takes 6 sprints to be completed by a team that has 20 story points’ velocity. Even though dividing 110 by 20 equals 5.5 sprints, the number of iterations should be an integer since the predetermined timebox of a sprint should not be changed. In Scrum, it’s possible to calculate the estimated number of sprints as long as the velocity of the team and the estimation of the workload are known. But, you need to keep in mind that this is an estimation rather than a commitment since changes could happen along the way.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A release of 110 story points takes 6 sprints to be completed by a team that has 20 story points’ velocity. Even though dividing 110 by 20 equals 5.5 sprints, the number of iterations should be an integer since the predetermined timebox of a sprint should not be changed. In Scrum, it’s possible to calculate the estimated number of sprints as long as the velocity of the team and the estimation of the workload are known. But, you need to keep in mind that this is an estimation rather than a commitment since changes could happen along the way.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The scope of business analysis is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The scope of business analysis is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Project-oriented<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project-oriented\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Product-oriented<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product-oriented\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product and project-oriented<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product and project-oriented\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>None of the above<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. None of the above\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Business analysis primarily concentrates on the features and functions that define a solution, making its scope product-oriented.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Project management involves overseeing all tasks required to deliver a product or service, making its scope both product-oriented and project-oriented.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Business analysis primarily concentrates on the features and functions that define a solution, making its scope product-oriented. Option C: Project management involves overseeing all tasks required to deliver a product or service, making its scope both product-oriented and project-oriented.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the below statements represents the most accurate definition of backlog refinement? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the below statements represents the most accurate definition of backlog refinement? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The process of creating the initial list of product requirements, formerly known as backlog grooming.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The process of creating the initial list of product requirements, formerly known as backlog grooming.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>When the product owner or team members review the backlog to make sure it has the proper items.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. When the product owner or team members review the backlog to make sure it has the proper items.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The continuous elaboration of project requirements to satisfy the stakeholders’ needs.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The continuous elaboration of project requirements to satisfy the stakeholders’ needs.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The continuous activity of writing, updating, and prioritizing requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The continuous activity of writing, updating, and prioritizing requirements.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Backlog refinement (formerly referred to as backlog grooming) occurs when the product owner along with some, or all of the team members checks the backlog to make sure it contains the proper items, that these items are prioritized, and that the ones at the top are ready to be delivered (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235). This activity is carried out regularly and can be either an officially scheduled meeting or an ongoing activity.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The process of developing the initial list of product requirements represents backlog elaboration or creation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, C, D Backlog refinement (formerly referred to as backlog grooming) occurs when the product owner along with some, or all of the team members checks the backlog to make sure it contains the proper items, that these items are prioritized, and that the ones at the top are ready to be delivered (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235). This activity is carried out regularly and can be either an officially scheduled meeting or an ongoing activity. Option A: The process of developing the initial list of product requirements represents backlog elaboration or creation.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A company must select one of two projects that have the same budget, but different returns and risk levels. Which tool or technique should be used in order to make the right decision?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A company must select one of two projects that have the same budget, but different returns and risk levels. Which tool or technique should be used in order to make the right decision?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision tree<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Decision tree\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tornado diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Tornado diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SWOT Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. SWOT Analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sensitivity analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sensitivity analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The decision tree analysis is used to support the identification and selection of the best course of action among several alternatives. Each of these alternative paths can have associated costs and risks, including both threats and opportunities. The decision tree reveals the expected monetary value of each branch, allowing the determination and selection of the optimal path (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The decision tree analysis is used to support the identification and selection of the best course of action among several alternatives. Each of these alternative paths can have associated costs and risks, including both threats and opportunities. The decision tree reveals the expected monetary value of each branch, allowing the determination and selection of the optimal path (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What does “cycle time” mean?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What does “cycle time” mean?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The duration of the project iterations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The duration of the project iterations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The time required to review a task<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The time required to review a task\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The time from the moment the team starts working on a task to the moment they complete it<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The time from the moment the team starts working on a task to the moment they complete it\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The time from the moment a task is created to the moment it’s completed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The time from the moment a task is created to the moment it’s completed\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The cycle time is how long it takes for the team to complete a task. It’s measured from the time they start working on the task.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Lead time, on the other hand, starts from the moment the task is added to the board (Agile Practice Guide, page 64).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The cycle time is how long it takes for the team to complete a task. It’s measured from the time they start working on the task. Option D: Lead time, on the other hand, starts from the moment the task is added to the board (Agile Practice Guide, page 64).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":26,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">Which statement is true about the following chart?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\" id=\\\"page_60\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Which statement is true about the following chart?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The figure represents a burnup chart of the remaining story points<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The figure represents a burnup chart of the remaining story points\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Throughout the iteration, the completed story points are always more than projected<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Throughout the iteration, the completed story points are always more than projected\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team planned 14 story points for the iteration which they completed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The team planned 14 story points for the iteration which they completed\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>3 story points are unfinished at the end of the iteration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 3 story points are unfinished at the end of the iteration\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">At the end of the seven-day iteration, 3 story points are left undone.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The team planned 14 story points, but they were only able to finish 11.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The figure represents a burndown chart and not a burnup chart.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> When the actual progress line of the chart is above the projected progress, it indicates that the team is finishing fewer story points than what they initially committed to.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D At the end of the seven-day iteration, 3 story points are left undone. Option C: The team planned 14 story points, but they were only able to finish 11. Option A: The figure represents a burndown chart and not a burnup chart. Option B: When the actual progress line of the chart is above the projected progress, it indicates that the team is finishing fewer story points than what they initially committed to.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":27,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Working with the predictive approach, which of the following is most true?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Working with the predictive approach, which of the following is most true?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lag can be determined by making a forward pass.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Lag can be determined by making a forward pass.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lag is the maximum amount of time a task can be delayed without delaying the early start of its successor.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Lag is the maximum amount of time a task can be delayed without delaying the early start of its successor.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lag is waiting time.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Lag is waiting time.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lag is the maximum amount of time a task can be delayed without delaying the whole project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Lag is the maximum amount of time a task can be delayed without delaying the whole project.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In a predictive approach, Lag is when an activity is complete and there is a delay before the subsequent activity starts (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 59). For example, in order to paint a room, you need to first apply the primer coating, then you have to let it dry for two days before applying the final coat of paint. These two days of waiting for the primer coat to dry are referred to as Lag Time.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In a predictive approach, Lag is when an activity is complete and there is a delay before the subsequent activity starts (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 59). For example, in order to paint a room, you need to first apply the primer coating, then you have to let it dry for two days before applying the final coat of paint. These two days of waiting for the primer coat to dry are referred to as Lag Time.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":28,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Before starting the project, the business analyst classifies stakeholders according to their level of power, interest, and influence. This step is referred to as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Before starting the project, the business analyst classifies stakeholders according to their level of power, interest, and influence. This step is referred to as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Stakeholder analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder identification<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder identification\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder monitoring<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder engagement\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since the question states that stakeholders were already identified and that the project hasn't started yet, stakeholder analysis is the right answer. Stakeholder analysis refers to the classification of all project stakeholders in order to ensure efficient engagement later on.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Stakeholder engagement takes place in the execution process group and it involves: communicating and collaborating with stakeholders to meet their expectations, addressing issues, and fostering appropriate stakeholder involvement.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Stakeholder monitoring implies assessing stakeholders’ satisfaction and whether their engagement plan is effective or it needs to be updated (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 11-12-14).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Since the question states that stakeholders were already identified and that the project hasn't started yet, stakeholder analysis is the right answer. Stakeholder analysis refers to the classification of all project stakeholders in order to ensure efficient engagement later on. Option D: Stakeholder engagement takes place in the execution process group and it involves: communicating and collaborating with stakeholders to meet their expectations, addressing issues, and fostering appropriate stakeholder involvement. Option C: Stakeholder monitoring implies assessing stakeholders’ satisfaction and whether their engagement plan is effective or it needs to be updated (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 11-12-14).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":29,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following best describes business analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following best describes business analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to deliver the project solutions for a project<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to deliver the project solutions for a project .\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Activities performed to support the identification and analysis of requirements and the identification of solutions relevant to one or many projects.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Activities performed to support the identification and analysis of requirements and the identification of solutions relevant to one or many projects.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Business analysis involves activities that support the delivery of solutions aligned with business objectives, ensuring continuous value for the organization. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 389)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> “An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes” is a description of the Project Management Office (PMO). The PMO is responsible for standardizing and overseeing project management practices within an organization, not specifically for performing business analysis.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> “The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals” is a description of portfolio management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to deliver the project solutions for a project” is a description of project management. Project management involves applying various skills, tools, and techniques to complete project tasks and deliver solutions. While business analysis supports project management by defining requirements and solutions, it is not the same as managing the entire project, which is the role of a project manager.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Business analysis involves activities that support the delivery of solutions aligned with business objectives, ensuring continuous value for the organization. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 389) Option A: “An organizational structure that aims to standardize project-related governance processes” is a description of the Project Management Office (PMO). The PMO is responsible for standardizing and overseeing project management practices within an organization, not specifically for performing business analysis. Option B: “The collection of programs that have been grouped to achieve strategic business goals” is a description of portfolio management. Option C: “The application of knowledge, skills, tools, and techniques to project activities to deliver the project solutions for a project” is a description of project management. Project management involves applying various skills, tools, and techniques to complete project tasks and deliver solutions. While business analysis supports project management by defining requirements and solutions, it is not the same as managing the entire project, which is the role of a project manager.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":30,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In a weak matrix organization, a project manager discovers that the assigned team lacks the necessary skills for the project. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a weak matrix organization, a project manager discovers that the assigned team lacks the necessary skills for the project. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue a change request to get a more qualified team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Issue a change request to get a more qualified team.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiate with the functional manager in order to obtain the required team members.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Negotiate with the functional manager in order to obtain the required team members.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Take the matter to the project sponsor.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Take the matter to the project sponsor.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use their legitimate power by informing the organization that they will not perform the project without the needed resources.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Use their legitimate power by informing the organization that they will not perform the project without the needed resources.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager's power is considerably low in a weak matrix organization. In fact, they are rather considered a coordinator or an expediter. It’s up to the functional manager to assign resources in such organizations. Therefore, the only solution to obtain the needed resources in this situation is by negotiating your requirements with the functional manager.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A project manager's power is considerably low in a weak matrix organization. In fact, they are rather considered a coordinator or an expediter. It’s up to the functional manager to assign resources in such organizations. Therefore, the only solution to obtain the needed resources in this situation is by negotiating your requirements with the functional manager.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":31,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A product owner who’s new to the agile approach wrote the following user story: “As a customer, I want a new functionality so that I can achieve a 50% increase in sales”. The project manager found the user story to be deficient, explaining to the product owner that:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A product owner who’s new to the agile approach wrote the following user story: “As a customer, I want a new functionality so that I can achieve a 50% increase in sales”. The project manager found the user story to be deficient, explaining to the product owner that:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The user story should follow a common structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The user story should follow a common structure\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The user story should be specific and testable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The user story should be specific and testable\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The user story should not include financial values<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The user story should not include financial values\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The user story should be time-bounded<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The user story should be time-bounded\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The user story written by the product owner is not specific and cannot be tested.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A good user story should be:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“I” Independent (of all others)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“N” Negotiable<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“V” Valuable<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“E” Estimable (to an acceptable approximation)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“S” Small (to fit within an iteration)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">“T” Testable<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">(PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 223)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Even if it’s written in a user story format it’s vague and unclear. The product owner must specify what new functionality they were looking to develop.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> It’s possible to include financial values in a user story as long as they contribute to making it more clear and more understandable.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A goal can be time-bound, i.e., a SMART goal, but a user story is not bounded by time.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The user story written by the product owner is not specific and cannot be tested. A good user story should be: “I” Independent (of all others) “N” Negotiable “V” Valuable “E” Estimable (to an acceptable approximation) “S” Small (to fit within an iteration) “T” Testable (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 223) Option A: Even if it’s written in a user story format it’s vague and unclear. The product owner must specify what new functionality they were looking to develop. Option C: It’s possible to include financial values in a user story as long as they contribute to making it more clear and more understandable. Option D: A goal can be time-bound, i.e., a SMART goal, but a user story is not bounded by time.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":32,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A product owner creates a release plan based on a projected team velocity of 50 story points. However, during the first two sprints, the team completed 37 points in sprint 1 and 35 story points in sprint 2. What should the agile project manager do in this situation? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A product owner creates a release plan based on a projected team velocity of 50 story points. However, during the first two sprints, the team completed 37 points in sprint 1 and 35 story points in sprint 2. What should the agile project manager do in this situation? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the product owner that, based on available empirical data, the release plan could not be achieved.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Inform the product owner that, based on available empirical data, the release plan could not be achieved.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use their leadership skills to motivate their team to reach the estimated velocity.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use their leadership skills to motivate their team to reach the estimated velocity.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Extend the duration of the sprint until the 50 story points are completed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Extend the duration of the sprint until the 50 story points are completed.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Study with the product owner the possibility of adding more resources to the team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Study with the product owner the possibility of adding more resources to the team.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Scrum uses empirical data to measure work progress, therefore the project manager should let the product owner know that, based on current performance, the release plan is not feasible. The product manager can update the release plan or study with the project manager the possibility of adding more resources to the team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The capacity of the team is around 36 story points, and it wouldn’t be possible to motivate the team to consistently reach 50 points on each sprint.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A sprint has a timeboxed duration which should not be extended for any reason.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, D Scrum uses empirical data to measure work progress, therefore the project manager should let the product owner know that, based on current performance, the release plan is not feasible. The product manager can update the release plan or study with the project manager the possibility of adding more resources to the team. Option B: The capacity of the team is around 36 story points, and it wouldn’t be possible to motivate the team to consistently reach 50 points on each sprint. Option C: A sprint has a timeboxed duration which should not be extended for any reason.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":33,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project team member notices that some requirements are missing from the project documentation. The project manager asks the team member to resolve the issue. What artifacts can the team member add to properly reflect the requirements statement? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team member notices that some requirements are missing from the project documentation. The project manager asks the team member to resolve the issue. What artifacts can the team member add to properly reflect the requirements statement? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Use cases<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use cases\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. User stories\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gantt chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Gantt chart\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Visual models<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Visual models\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B, C, E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Requirements statement can be expressed in artifacts, such as use cases, user stories, backlog items, and visual models.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The risk register is a tool to identify, assess, and manage risks throughout the project. It does not capture requirements but focuses on potential risks that could affect the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Gantt chart is a tool used to visualize the project schedule, it does not express any requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, C, E Requirements statement can be expressed in artifacts, such as use cases, user stories, backlog items, and visual models. Option A: The risk register is a tool to identify, assess, and manage risks throughout the project. It does not capture requirements but focuses on potential risks that could affect the project. Option D: Gantt chart is a tool used to visualize the project schedule, it does not express any requirements.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":34,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">Three manufacturing lines are producing 5 mm diameter cylindrical steel bars. In order to perform a quality inspection, the project manager takes 10 random bars from each line. The following are the inspection results in mm measurements. The results of  Line 1 can be described as:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Three manufacturing lines are producing 5 mm diameter cylindrical steel bars. In order to perform a quality inspection, the project manager takes 10 random bars from each line. The following are the inspection results in mm measurements. The results of  Line 1 can be described as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accurate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Accurate\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Precise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Precise\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Both accurate and precise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Both accurate and precise\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Neither accurate nor precise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Neither accurate nor precise\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The results are precise because all measurements are close to 4.45mm (+ or - 5mm). Precision entails delivering end-products with similar dimensions, which may or may not be close to the required dimensions. Precise measurements are not necessarily close to the target value; they’re just close to one another.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Accuracy implies creating products with close dimensions to requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The results are precise because all measurements are close to 4.45mm (+ or - 5mm). Precision entails delivering end-products with similar dimensions, which may or may not be close to the required dimensions. Precise measurements are not necessarily close to the target value; they’re just close to one another. Option A: Accuracy implies creating products with close dimensions to requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":35,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is evaluating a potential industrial project. To determine whether its anticipated financial gains will outweigh its present-day investment, the project manager uses the Net Present Value (NPV) as an effective tool to help her determine whether the project will be profitable or not. For instance, NPV &gt; 0 means:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is evaluating a potential industrial project. To determine whether its anticipated financial gains will outweigh its present-day investment, the project manager uses the Net Present Value (NPV) as an effective tool to help her determine whether the project will be profitable or not. For instance, NPV > 0 means:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project will lose money<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project will lose money\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project will break even<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project will break even\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is profitable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project is profitable\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>We can’t know until the ROI is calculated<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. We can’t know until the ROI is calculated\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The larger the Net Present Value (NPV), the more profitable the project will be for the organization. A positive NPV indicates that the investment is worthwhile.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The larger the Net Present Value (NPV), the more profitable the project will be for the organization. A positive NPV indicates that the investment is worthwhile.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":36,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">All of the following imply servant leadership characteristics, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"All of the following imply servant leadership characteristics, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Promoting team members' professional growth<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Promoting team members' professional growth\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prioritizing the team needs ahead of everything else<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Prioritizing the team needs ahead of everything else\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Succession planning by developing future servant leaders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Succession planning by developing future servant leaders\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Taking instructions from the team concerning project work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Taking instructions from the team concerning project work\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A servant leader promotes team growth, prioritizes their needs, and plans for successors by developing future servant leaders. This leadership style, however, does not entail that the project manager has to take instructions from their team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A servant leader promotes team growth, prioritizes their needs, and plans for successors by developing future servant leaders. This leadership style, however, does not entail that the project manager has to take instructions from their team.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":37,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project’s performance measurements are calculated based on the following information: EV = $2,000 and AC = $1,000. What is the status of the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project’s performance measurements are calculated based on the following information: EV = $2,000 and AC = $1,000. What is the status of the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is ahead of schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is ahead of schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is behind schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project is behind schedule\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is under budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project is under budget\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is over budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project is over budget\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The CPI (Cost Performance Index) is a measure of the conformance of the actual work completed (EV, Earned Value) with the incurred Actual Cost (AC): CPI = EV / AC = $2,000 / $1,000 = 2 which means that the project is under budget<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, B:<\\/span> The Schedule Performance Index measures the conformance of actual progress to the planned progress (SPI = EV / PV). Since the PV is unknown, we can’t find out if the project is behind or ahead of schedule.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The CPI (Cost Performance Index) is a measure of the conformance of the actual work completed (EV, Earned Value) with the incurred Actual Cost (AC): CPI = EV / AC = $2,000 / $1,000 = 2 which means that the project is under budget . Options A, B: The Schedule Performance Index measures the conformance of actual progress to the planned progress (SPI = EV / PV). Since the PV is unknown, we can’t find out if the project is behind or ahead of schedule.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":38,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is developing the business case of a green transportation project. To do so, they decide to use the SWOT technique. How should the project manager apply this technique<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is developing the business case of a green transportation project. To do so, they decide to use the SWOT technique. How should the project manager apply this technique ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Follow a Plan-Do-Check-Act cycle (PDCA Cycle)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Follow a Plan-Do-Check-Act cycle (PDCA Cycle)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Assess the business model using expert judgment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Assess the business model using expert judgment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Identify the project's strengths and weaknesses ​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Identify the project's strengths and weaknesses\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct a benefit/cost analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conduct a benefit/cost analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">SWOT stands for Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats. It’s a tool that project managers use to assess the opportunities and threats they might face, as well as their projects’ strengths and weaknesses (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 177).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The PDCA cycle is a quality management technique to control and continuously improve processes and products.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> Assessing the project’s business model or conducting a benefit/cost analysis could be part of developing the business case, but both methods have a different purpose from the SWOT technique.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C SWOT stands for Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats. It’s a tool that project managers use to assess the opportunities and threats they might face, as well as their projects’ strengths and weaknesses (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 177). Option A: The PDCA cycle is a quality management technique to control and continuously improve processes and products. Options B & D: Assessing the project’s business model or conducting a benefit/cost analysis could be part of developing the business case, but both methods have a different purpose from the SWOT technique.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":39,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The product owner should sort the product backlog items by placing:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The product owner should sort the product backlog items by placing:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The easiest items at the top<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The easiest items at the top\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The less valuable items at the bottom<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The less valuable items at the bottom\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The most recent items at the top<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The most recent items at the top\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The less clear items at the top<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The less clear items at the top\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The product owner is responsible for placing the clearest and most valuable items at the top of the product backlog. Consequently, less valuable items will be dragged to the bottom.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> Product backlog items should not be organized chronologically or according to their difficulty level.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The product owner is responsible for placing the clearest and most valuable items at the top of the product backlog. Consequently, less valuable items will be dragged to the bottom. Options A & C: Product backlog items should not be organized chronologically or according to their difficulty level.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":40,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager is leading a complex project with a very demanding sponsor who wants frequent updates on project progress and future plans. What’s the best way for the project manager to communicate with the sponsor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a complex project with a very demanding sponsor who wants frequent updates on project progress and future plans. What’s the best way for the project manager to communicate with the sponsor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Send a comprehensive monthly report detailing all project progress aspects regarding scope, schedule, cost, risks, etc.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Send a comprehensive monthly report detailing all project progress aspects regarding scope, schedule, cost, risks, etc.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule a monthly face-to-face meeting to discuss the project status.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Schedule a monthly face-to-face meeting to discuss the project status.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Set up weekly or bi-weekly meetings and inform the sponsor that they are welcome to attend daily standups.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Set up weekly or bi-weekly meetings and inform the sponsor that they are welcome to attend daily standups.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hold a bi-weekly meeting and give the sponsor access to the project management software for real-time updates on the project status.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Hold a bi-weekly meeting and give the sponsor access to the project management software for real-time updates on the project status.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since the project is complex, frequent communication is required. Therefore, the best option is to schedule regular meetings once or twice a week, with the possibility of attending standup meetings to get daily updates.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Monthly meetings, even if they’re face-to-face, are not efficient for complex projects.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Giving access to the project management software is considered pull communication since the sponsor has to seek information themself. Pull communication might not be sufficient for high-power demanding stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Since the project is complex, frequent communication is required. Therefore, the best option is to schedule regular meetings once or twice a week, with the possibility of attending standup meetings to get daily updates. Option B: Monthly meetings, even if they’re face-to-face, are not efficient for complex projects. Option D: Giving access to the project management software is considered pull communication since the sponsor has to seek information themself. Pull communication might not be sufficient for high-power demanding stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":41,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In a typical communication context, elements interfering with the transmission and understanding of the project manager’s message are called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a typical communication context, elements interfering with the transmission and understanding of the project manager’s message are called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Medium<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Medium\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Noise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Noise\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Decode<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decode\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In a typical communication context, and according to the sender-receiver model, anything that obstructs the transmission and comprehension of a message is called noise.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> The key components of the communication process also include encoding thoughts or ideas, a message as the output of encoding, a medium to transmit the message, and decoding the message back into meaningful information.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B In a typical communication context, and according to the sender-receiver model, anything that obstructs the transmission and comprehension of a message is called noise. Options A & C: The key components of the communication process also include encoding thoughts or ideas, a message as the output of encoding, a medium to transmit the message, and decoding the message back into meaningful information.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":42,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following tools and techniques are used for stakeholders analysis? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following tools and techniques are used for stakeholders analysis? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. RACI matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision tree<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Decision tree\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Persona analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Persona analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus groups<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Focus groups\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A &amp; <span><\\/span>C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In order to properly analyze the project stakeholders, a business analyst can use one or more of these tools (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 115):<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Job analysis:<\\/span> This technique is employed to determine the skills, qualifications, and competencies needed for a particular job or role.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Persona analysis:<\\/span> Persona analysis involves creating a fictional character, known as a persona, to represent an individual or a group of stakeholders within a user class.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Stakeholder maps:<\\/span> Stakeholder maps can include matrices that illustrate the influence and impact of each stakeholder.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>RACI matrix:<\\/span> This a tool designed to clarify stakeholder responsibilities by mapping out who is Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed for each project activity. It helps ensure effective communication and management of stakeholder expectations throughout the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A decision tree is a tool used for decision-making and analyzing different outcomes of various choices.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Focus groups assemble prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to gather insights into their expectations and attitudes toward a proposed solution.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A & C In order to properly analyze the project stakeholders, a business analyst can use one or more of these tools (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 115): ● Job analysis: This technique is employed to determine the skills, qualifications, and competencies needed for a particular job or role. ● Persona analysis: Persona analysis involves creating a fictional character, known as a persona, to represent an individual or a group of stakeholders within a user class. ● Stakeholder maps: Stakeholder maps can include matrices that illustrate the influence and impact of each stakeholder. ● RACI matrix: This a tool designed to clarify stakeholder responsibilities by mapping out who is Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed for each project activity. It helps ensure effective communication and management of stakeholder expectations throughout the project. Option B: A decision tree is a tool used for decision-making and analyzing different outcomes of various choices. Option D: Focus groups assemble prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to gather insights into their expectations and attitudes toward a proposed solution.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":43,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a one-year project. Five months into the execution phase, %50 of the project work is completed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-0\\\">What is the project’s SPI and status<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a one-year project. Five months into the execution phase, %50 of the project work is completed. What is the project’s SPI and status ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The SPI is 0.83 and the project is behind schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The SPI is 0.83 and the project is behind schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The SPI is 0.83 and the project is ahead of schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The SPI is 0.83 and the project is ahead of schedule\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The SPI is 1.2 and the project is behind schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The SPI is 1.2 and the project is behind schedule\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The SPI is 1.2 and the project is ahead of schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The SPI is 1.2 and the project is ahead of schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">EV = % of completed work X BAC (Budget at Completion) = (6/12) X BAC.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since the project manager is 5 months into the project, then the PV = (5/12) X BAC. Doing the math, SPI = EV / PV = 6 / 5 = 1.2.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">You can also conclude that the project is ahead of schedule without doing any math since half of the work is done before reaching half of the project duration. Since the project is ahead of schedule, you should just select the answer where the SPI is greater than 1.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D EV = % of completed work X BAC (Budget at Completion) = (6/12) X BAC. Since the project manager is 5 months into the project, then the PV = (5/12) X BAC. Doing the math, SPI = EV / PV = 6 / 5 = 1.2. You can also conclude that the project is ahead of schedule without doing any math since half of the work is done before reaching half of the project duration. Since the project is ahead of schedule, you should just select the answer where the SPI is greater than 1.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":44,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a workshop about the Agile approach, the project manager stated that Agile teams should be cross-functional and self-organizing, explaining that:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a workshop about the Agile approach, the project manager stated that Agile teams should be cross-functional and self-organizing, explaining that:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Each member of the team should be cross-functional and self-organized.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Each member of the team should be cross-functional and self-organized.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Agile team should have all the required skills to deliver the product on their own.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Agile team should have all the required skills to deliver the product on their own.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Agile team should have complementary skill sets and be able to organize the backlog by themselves.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The Agile team should have complementary skill sets and be able to organize the backlog by themselves.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Agile team should self-organize to acquire the necessary skills to be cross-functional.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The Agile team should self-organize to acquire the necessary skills to be cross-functional.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A cross-functional team is a group of individuals who acquire different substantial skill sets that are enough to accomplish their common goal proficiently. A self-organizing team is autonomous in the sense that it does not rely on any outsiders to figure out how to best accomplish its work. This does not mean that each team member possesses all of the necessary skills for delivering the product; rather, they just need to be competent in their area of expertise.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A cross-functional team is a group of individuals who acquire different substantial skill sets that are enough to accomplish their common goal proficiently. A self-organizing team is autonomous in the sense that it does not rely on any outsiders to figure out how to best accomplish its work. This does not mean that each team member possesses all of the necessary skills for delivering the product; rather, they just need to be competent in their area of expertise.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":45,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager plans to discuss with her manager the need for additional resources to handle complex tasks her team cannot perform. These resources will be released from the project once the tasks are completed. Which skills are most crucial for the project manager in this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager plans to discuss with her manager the need for additional resources to handle complex tasks her team cannot perform. These resources will be released from the project once the tasks are completed. Which skills are most crucial for the project manager in this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning skills to determine resource requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planning skills to determine resource requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interpersonal skills to persuade her manager to allocate additional resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Interpersonal skills to persuade her manager to allocate additional resources\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interviewing skills to recruit the necessary resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interviewing skills to recruit the necessary resources\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Technical skills to address the risk associated with adding more resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Technical skills to address the risk associated with adding more resources\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Trying to convince upper management requires the use of interpersonal skills, which are often needed when acquiring resources.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project manager may lack planning skills since she didn’t identify the resource requirement from the beginning, but this situation does not tackle this aspect or the need to respond to the risk associated with adding more resources. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> In case the manager accepts her request, the project manager may not need to go through the hiring process if resources are already available within the organization.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Trying to convince upper management requires the use of interpersonal skills, which are often needed when acquiring resources. Option A: The project manager may lack planning skills since she didn’t identify the resource requirement from the beginning, but this situation does not tackle this aspect or the need to respond to the risk associated with adding more resources. Option C: In case the manager accepts her request, the project manager may not need to go through the hiring process if resources are already available within the organization.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":46,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">To adopt an agile mindset, the project team can use all of the following questions while developing the product, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To adopt an agile mindset, the project team can use all of the following questions while developing the product, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>What work can be avoided to only focus on high-priority tasks?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. What work can be avoided to only focus on high-priority tasks?\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>How can the Agile team work in a predictable manner?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. How can the Agile team work in a predictable manner?\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>What work should be prioritized in order to obtain early feedback?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. What work should be prioritized in order to obtain early feedback?\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>How can servant leadership help the achievement of project goals?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. How can servant leadership help the achievement of project goals?\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Agile teams don't focus on how to predict the project work; instead, they try to focus on high-priority tasks, getting early feedback, and adopting the servant leadership approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Agile teams don't focus on how to predict the project work; instead, they try to focus on high-priority tasks, getting early feedback, and adopting the servant leadership approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":47,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst’s role involves extensive upfront planning and detailed requirements gathering primarily in the early stages of a project. In which development approach the business analyst is working?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst’s role involves extensive upfront planning and detailed requirements gathering primarily in the early stages of a project. In which development approach the business analyst is working?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iterative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Iterative\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Adaptive\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The predictive approach relies on a well-defined plan and aims to minimize changes once the project is underway.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The adaptive approach emphasizes flexibility and adaptability. Requirements are continuously evolving based on stakeholder feedback and changes in project conditions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The predictive approach relies on a well-defined plan and aims to minimize changes once the project is underway. Option D: The adaptive approach emphasizes flexibility and adaptability. Requirements are continuously evolving based on stakeholder feedback and changes in project conditions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":48,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager, who manages an online e-learning platform, decided to make all new release information accessible to the platform members under the “News” section on the website. What type of communication is the project manager intends to use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager, who manages an online e-learning platform, decided to make all new release information accessible to the platform members under the “News” section on the website. What type of communication is the project manager intends to use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Push communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Push communication\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Interactive communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Interactive communication\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Pull communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Pull communication\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Proactive communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Proactive communication\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Pull communication is a communication type where access to the information is provided, however, the receiver must proactively seek out and retrieve this information. When the communication is solely for informative purposes, pull communication should be used. It will have little to no impact on the project if the recipients do not read it. According to the PMI process groups guide: “Pull communication is used for large complex information sets, or for large audiences, and requires the recipients to access the content at their own discretion subject to security procedures. These methods include web portals, intranet sites, e-learning, lessons learned databases, or knowledge repositories.” (PMI Process groups Guide, page 253)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The PMBOK Guide defined three types of communication: interactive, push, and pull. Proactive communication is a made-up term.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Pull communication is a communication type where access to the information is provided, however, the receiver must proactively seek out and retrieve this information. When the communication is solely for informative purposes, pull communication should be used. It will have little to no impact on the project if the recipients do not read it. According to the PMI process groups guide: “Pull communication is used for large complex information sets, or for large audiences, and requires the recipients to access the content at their own discretion subject to security procedures. These methods include web portals, intranet sites, e-learning, lessons learned databases, or knowledge repositories.” (PMI Process groups Guide, page 253) Option D: The PMBOK Guide defined three types of communication: interactive, push, and pull. Proactive communication is a made-up term.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":49,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager attended a leadership training workshop. The trainer listed the characteristics of servant leaders, then mentioned some examples of a servant leader’s behavioral traits, such as: (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager attended a leadership training workshop. The trainer listed the characteristics of servant leaders, then mentioned some examples of a servant leader’s behavioral traits, such as: (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Helping a team member write a professional email to a stakeholder in order to get key information.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Helping a team member write a professional email to a stakeholder in order to get key information.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rewarding high-performing employees in order to motivate them.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Rewarding high-performing employees in order to motivate them.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Checking up on a team member to find out why they’ve suddenly become an introvert.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Checking up on a team member to find out why they’ve suddenly become an introvert.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inspiring their team with success stories.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Inspiring their team with success stories.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Helping someone do a task properly and focusing on people’s well-being are the main behavioral aspects and characteristics of servant leaders. However, rewarding high-performing employees is considered transactional leadership, whereas inspiring people falls under the charismatic leadership style.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C Helping someone do a task properly and focusing on people’s well-being are the main behavioral aspects and characteristics of servant leaders. However, rewarding high-performing employees is considered transactional leadership, whereas inspiring people falls under the charismatic leadership style.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":50,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager has just taken over an ongoing project for creating a newborns’ essentials brand. Items made of fabric are manufactured by external vendors. To get to know all vendors involved in the project, the project manager should check out:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has just taken over an ongoing project for creating a newborns’ essentials brand. Items made of fabric are manufactured by external vendors. To get to know all vendors involved in the project, the project manager should check out:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RFQs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. RFQs\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Vendors’ proposals<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Vendors’ proposals\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder engagement plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The stakeholder register document contains all relevant information concerning the project stakeholders including their influence, interest, involvement, and potential impact on the project’s success. External vendors are considered project stakeholders and therefore they should take part in the stakeholder register. The project manager should refer to this document whenever they need any information concerning both internal and external stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The stakeholder register document contains all relevant information concerning the project stakeholders including their influence, interest, involvement, and potential impact on the project’s success. External vendors are considered project stakeholders and therefore they should take part in the stakeholder register. The project manager should refer to this document whenever they need any information concerning both internal and external stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":51,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What are the areas of emotional intelligence? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What are the areas of emotional intelligence? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Social-awareness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Social-awareness\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-awareness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Self-awareness\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Self-management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Culture awareness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Culture awareness\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Problem-solving<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Problem-solving\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Social awareness involves empathy and understanding the emotions of others. It encompasses the ability to interpret nonverbal cues and body language.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Self-awareness is the capacity to objectively evaluate oneself. It involves an understanding of one’s emotions, goals, motivations, strengths, and weaknesses. Self-management, also known as <span><\\/span>self-regulation, is the ability to control and redirect disruptive feelings and impulses. It is the ability to think before acting, suspending snap judgments and impulsive decisions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C Social awareness involves empathy and understanding the emotions of others. It encompasses the ability to interpret nonverbal cues and body language. Self-awareness is the capacity to objectively evaluate oneself. It involves an understanding of one’s emotions, goals, motivations, strengths, and weaknesses. Self-management, also known as self-regulation, is the ability to control and redirect disruptive feelings and impulses. It is the ability to think before acting, suspending snap judgments and impulsive decisions.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":52,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to lead a megaproject that requires experts and resources from different countries. Unable to predict worldwide epidemics, the project team is worried about facing another event like CoronaVirus that might cause delays and cost overruns. What should the project manager do during the risk planning phase? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to lead a megaproject that requires experts and resources from different countries. Unable to predict worldwide epidemics, the project team is worried about facing another event like CoronaVirus that might cause delays and cost overruns. What should the project manager do during the risk planning phase? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add the risk to the risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Add the risk to the risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Perform a qualitative risk analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Perform a qualitative risk analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add the risk to the issue lo<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Add the risk to the issue lo g\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitor the development of the risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Monitor the development of the risk\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project team should perform a qualitative risk analysis. If they find that the risk must be prioritized, a detailed risk response should be then developed. All identified risks should be added to the risk register.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> During the project execution, all occurring issues are noted in the issue log.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Monitoring the risk development is undertaken during the execution phase too, not the planning phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B The project team should perform a qualitative risk analysis. If they find that the risk must be prioritized, a detailed risk response should be then developed. All identified risks should be added to the risk register. Option C: During the project execution, all occurring issues are noted in the issue log. Option D: Monitoring the risk development is undertaken during the execution phase too, not the planning phase.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":53,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of these documents comprises thorough descriptions of work packages?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of these documents comprises thorough descriptions of work packages?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>WBS<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. WBS\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>WBS Dictionary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. WBS Dictionary\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Activity List<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Activity List\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scope management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The planned work is included in the lowest level of the WBS components, known as work packages. Detailed information on work packages, such as descriptions, owners, prerequisites, successors, due dates, etc. is included in the Work Breakdown Structure Dictionary (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 253).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The planned work is included in the lowest level of the WBS components, known as work packages. Detailed information on work packages, such as descriptions, owners, prerequisites, successors, due dates, etc. is included in the Work Breakdown Structure Dictionary (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 253).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":54,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Who can sign the project charter? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who can sign the project charter? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Steering Committee<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Steering Committee\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Office (PMO)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project Management Office (PMO)\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Project Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Project Team\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Projects get authorized by someone external to the project such as the sponsor, PMO, or steering committee (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The project manager cannot sign the charter to authorize himself to start executing the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> The project team doesn't have the power to sign the project charter.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, D Projects get authorized by someone external to the project such as the sponsor, PMO, or steering committee (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 184). Option C: The project manager cannot sign the charter to authorize himself to start executing the project. Option E: The project team doesn't have the power to sign the project charter.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":55,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Knowledge garnered through personal experience is the most difficult to express, articulate, or write down. This type of knowledge is known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Knowledge garnered through personal experience is the most difficult to express, articulate, or write down. This type of knowledge is known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Explicit knowledge<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Explicit knowledge\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tacit knowledge<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Tacit knowledge\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tangible knowledge<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Tangible knowledge\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formal knowledge<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Formal knowledge\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Tacit knowledge, aka implicit knowledge, is the type of knowledge that can’t be transferred to another person by means of writing or verbalizing. Examples of tacit knowledge include insights, beliefs, experience, and know-how.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The opposite of tacit knowledge is explicit, formal, or codified knowledge (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 70).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Tacit knowledge, aka implicit knowledge, is the type of knowledge that can’t be transferred to another person by means of writing or verbalizing. Examples of tacit knowledge include insights, beliefs, experience, and know-how. Option A: The opposite of tacit knowledge is explicit, formal, or codified knowledge (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 70).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":56,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">What type of requirements are expressed in the form of a business case?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What type of requirements are expressed in the form of a business case?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transition requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Transition requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholders requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Business requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Solution requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Solution requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Business requirements outline the high-level needs and objectives of the organization, including key issues or opportunities that the project aims to address. They provide a rationale for undertaking the project, typically articulated through a business case that highlights the anticipated benefits and strategic value<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Transition requirements describe the procedures for deploying and releasing a solution into production. These requirements are specific to the deployment phase and are temporary; they will not need to be executed again once the project is complete.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Stakeholder requirements outline the specific needs and expectations of individual stakeholders or stakeholder groups.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Solution requirements outline the specific attributes of a solution, including the features and functionalities of a product. These requirements address both business and stakeholder needs and must be detailed enough to guide the design and development of the solution effectively. Solution requirements have two subcategories: functional and non-functional requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Business requirements outline the high-level needs and objectives of the organization, including key issues or opportunities that the project aims to address. They provide a rationale for undertaking the project, typically articulated through a business case that highlights the anticipated benefits and strategic value . Option A: Transition requirements describe the procedures for deploying and releasing a solution into production. These requirements are specific to the deployment phase and are temporary; they will not need to be executed again once the project is complete. Option B: Stakeholder requirements outline the specific needs and expectations of individual stakeholders or stakeholder groups. Option D: Solution requirements outline the specific attributes of a solution, including the features and functionalities of a product. These requirements address both business and stakeholder needs and must be detailed enough to guide the design and development of the solution effectively. Solution requirements have two subcategories: functional and non-functional requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":57,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">How is the cost variance measured?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"How is the cost variance measured?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>EV / AC<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. EV / AC\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>BAC / EV<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. BAC / EV\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>EV - AC<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. EV - AC\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>BAC / AC<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. BAC / AC\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>BAC - AC<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. BAC - AC\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Cost variance is the difference between the estimated cost and the actual cost. Its formula is EV - AC<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Cost variance is the difference between the estimated cost and the actual cost. Its formula is EV - AC\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":58,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Due to high levels of uncertainty, the project manager opts for the rolling wave method for the project planning. How is this method useful in this case<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Due to high levels of uncertainty, the project manager opts for the rolling wave method for the project planning. How is this method useful in this case ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It will help the project manager determine which activities are more important to prioritize<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It will help the project manager determine which activities are more important to prioritize\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​It will help the project manager organize the project’s activities and tasks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It will help the project manager organize the project’s activities and tasks\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​It will help the project manager determine the sequencing of a large number of activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It will help the project manager determine the sequencing of a large number of activities\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​It will help the project manager reach the proper level of detail in each work package at the right time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It will help the project manager reach the proper level of detail in each work package at the right time\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Rolling wave is a project planning method that consists of a gradual elaboration of details to the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) over time. Near-term deliverables are decomposed into individual components (work packages) that are broken down to the greatest degree of detail. Long-term deliverables, on the other hand, are identified more broadly. In this way, rolling wave planning allows work to progress on current and near-term deliverables while the planning for potential work packages continues.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A, B, C:<\\/span> The Rolling wave method is used to address uncertainty rather than prioritizing, organizing, or sequencing activities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Rolling wave is a project planning method that consists of a gradual elaboration of details to the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) over time. Near-term deliverables are decomposed into individual components (work packages) that are broken down to the greatest degree of detail. Long-term deliverables, on the other hand, are identified more broadly. In this way, rolling wave planning allows work to progress on current and near-term deliverables while the planning for potential work packages continues. Options A, B, C: The Rolling wave method is used to address uncertainty rather than prioritizing, organizing, or sequencing activities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 249).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":59,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project has 5 iteration cycles, as the project advances to the 3rd iteration, the number of user stories in the backlog decreases significantly. What’s the potential cause of the decrease?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project has 5 iteration cycles, as the project advances to the 3rd iteration, the number of user stories in the backlog decreases significantly. What’s the potential cause of the decrease?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team entered a technical sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The team entered a technical sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A new tool is used to calculate the velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A new tool is used to calculate the velocity\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team refined the backlog and removed lower-priority stories<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The team refined the backlog and removed lower-priority stories\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team added more features to the product backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The team added more features to the product backlog\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">As the project progresses, the team reviews and updates the backlog. During this refinement, lower-priority or less valuable user stories might be removed or deprioritized to focus on higher-priority tasks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C As the project progresses, the team reviews and updates the backlog. During this refinement, lower-priority or less valuable user stories might be removed or deprioritized to focus on higher-priority tasks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":60,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An agile project manager observes that several stakeholders have become disengaged; they rarely attend meetings or provide feedback and input. What can the project manager do to address this issue? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An agile project manager observes that several stakeholders have become disengaged; they rarely attend meetings or provide feedback and input. What can the project manager do to address this issue? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Send a reminder before each meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Send a reminder before each meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform stakeholders that they can provide their feedback anonymously<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Inform stakeholders that they can provide their feedback anonymously\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Value and show appreciation for everyone's ideas<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Value and show appreciation for everyone's ideas\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Demonstrate the working increments<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Demonstrate the working increments\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Most probably, stakeholders are losing interest in the project because their input or feedback is being disregarded, or they are not seeing any tangible progress. The project manager has to engage stakeholders by taking their feedback into consideration to show them that their ideas are valued. The project manager should also demonstrate working increments as early in the project lifecycle as possible. This is considered one of the advantages of the agile approach that stakeholders expect and appreciate.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> Sending reminders before each meeting or allowing for anonymous feedback does not yield more engagement as both options don’t address the root cause of the problem.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C, D Most probably, stakeholders are losing interest in the project because their input or feedback is being disregarded, or they are not seeing any tangible progress. The project manager has to engage stakeholders by taking their feedback into consideration to show them that their ideas are valued. The project manager should also demonstrate working increments as early in the project lifecycle as possible. This is considered one of the advantages of the agile approach that stakeholders expect and appreciate. Options A & B: Sending reminders before each meeting or allowing for anonymous feedback does not yield more engagement as both options don’t address the root cause of the problem.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":61,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">After multiple negotiation sessions, all of the terms and details were agreed upon and the seller finally got the 18-month building project contract for $715,500. What type of contract is used in this scenario?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After multiple negotiation sessions, all of the terms and details were agreed upon and the seller finally got the 18-month building project contract for $715,500. What type of contract is used in this scenario?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Time and Material<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Time and Material\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed Price<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Fixed Price\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Reimbursable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cost Reimbursable\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Plus Incentive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cost Plus Incentive\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Fixed price contracts are used for projects with clear requirements where a price is fixed in return for the seller’s services and/or products.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Time and Material (T&amp;M) contracts set a quote for an hourly rate plus the cost of materials instead of quoting a fixed price for the entire project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Cost-reimbursable contracts, on the other hand, reimburse the contractor for the actual costs they incur to provide their services and/or product, plus an additional fee.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A Cost Plus Incentive contract, for instance, is a cost-reimbursable contract that incentivizes the contractor to bring their best performance by completing the project under budget or before deadlines.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Fixed price contracts are used for projects with clear requirements where a price is fixed in return for the seller’s services and/or products. Option A: Time and Material (T&M) contracts set a quote for an hourly rate plus the cost of materials instead of quoting a fixed price for the entire project. Option C: Cost-reimbursable contracts, on the other hand, reimburse the contractor for the actual costs they incur to provide their services and/or product, plus an additional fee. Option D: A Cost Plus Incentive contract, for instance, is a cost-reimbursable contract that incentivizes the contractor to bring their best performance by completing the project under budget or before deadlines.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":62,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager decides to use the Five Whys method in order to investigate a dysfunctioning feature. Why did the project manager choose to use this specific technique?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager decides to use the Five Whys method in order to investigate a dysfunctioning feature. Why did the project manager choose to use this specific technique?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To identify the five main factors that caused the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To identify the five main factors that caused the issue\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To identify the root cause of the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To identify the root cause of the issue\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To identify the five members responsible for the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To identify the five members responsible for the issue\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To identify the five steps to take to resolve the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To identify the five steps to take to resolve the issue\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">As a problem-solving technique, the Five Whys is used to explore the underlying cause of a defect or an issue. By asking successive “Why?” questions, the team digs deep to figure out what went wrong and thus be able to determine how to properly address the problem and how to avoid similar issues in the future.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B As a problem-solving technique, the Five Whys is used to explore the underlying cause of a defect or an issue. By asking successive “Why?” questions, the team digs deep to figure out what went wrong and thus be able to determine how to properly address the problem and how to avoid similar issues in the future.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":63,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-0\\\">A project manager is leading a construction project. Throughout its execution, the project was influenced by both Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs) and Organizational Process Assets (OPAs). Match the following statements with the corresponding influence category:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
